Section Boundary Detection:

Start of a section:

- You will find a section identifier string, eg. 3.0 Exterior
- The next row from it, it will be the head columns: Description, Part Number, List Price, FRT, Installed Price. These headers are different for EN/FR sheets

End of the section criteria:

- The row that has data that comes before the very first all empty row from the section identifier, before reaching another section identifier.
- This should be very strict and clearly defined.

As per the current design, there will be no overlap of records between sections.

Challenge 1B: Packages/Kits Rollup (Honda-Specific)

Excel structure:
┌─────────────────────────────┐
│ 1.0 Packages and Kits │ ← Section header
├─────────────────────────────┤
│ Part | Desc | Price | Trims │
├─────────────────────────────┤
│ PKG-001 | Premium Package | [data] │ ← Parent package
│ PART-A | Item A in premium | $X │ ← Child item (indented or marker?)
│ PART-B | Item B in premium | $Y │ ← Child item
│ PKG-002 | Standard Package | [data] │ ← Parent package (new)
│ PART-C | Item C in standard | $Z │ ← Child item
└─────────────────────────────┘

Goal: Roll up to one row per package
└─ PKG-001 | Premium Package | [aggregated parts A+B] │
└─ PKG-002 | Standard Package | [aggregated parts C] │

This is the goal as described here,

- Parent row has children, children have no child rows.
- Children rows are characterized by: they are in the package section only, they are missing values in list price, FRT, INstalled PRice, and model columns,m and they come after a parent column that has description, and the rest of the compulsory columns filed (they will be defined). A parent can have 1 or more children, and you know the a part family has ended when you find another parent.
- We will keep parent numeric values like price, labour, etc.
- If parent row has part Number empty, count 2 columns from part number to the left (target column, Description, PartNumber), check if there's a value, if it's there take it, if it's not, log that. Column names will be diff by language version. It is expected that the partNumber will be in the backup column but it's possible not too.
- Yes, description values of all the children will be concatenated into the comment section of the parent row.
- If row looks like parent and child, we will need to flag it and pass it in the DQ report
- All this will take place until the package section is over.

Every action should be logged.

